From: Plain Browser
Subject: [branding] Install modes: product name, ProgIDs, fresh GUIDs

chromium_install_modes.h (install dir, user data dir, registry and ProgID names, Start menu name) now say Plain Browser.
Active Setup and toast activator GUIDs are new so a Plain Browser install cannot hijack those registrations of a real
Chromium on the same machine. The elevation service and tracing service CLSIDs/IIDs are left as upstream: they are
tied to generated IDL files. BRANDING and the UI strings are handled by scripts/apply-branding.py.
---
--- a/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
+++ b/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
@@ -21,10 +21,10 @@
 
 // The brand-specific product name to be included as a component of the install
 // and user data directory paths.
-inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Chromium";
+inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"PlainBrowser";
 
 // The brand-specific safe browsing client name.
-inline constexpr char kSafeBrowsingName[] = "chromium";
+inline constexpr char kSafeBrowsingName[] = "plainbrowser";
 
 // Note: This list of indices must be kept in sync with the brand-specific
 // resource strings in chrome/installer/util/prebuild/create_string_rc.
@@ -54,23 +54,22 @@
